  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 123 PM MDT Sat Oct 24 2026\n\nFor Monday onward into the end of the week, it should primarily be \ndry with cooler temperatures over the region (60s/L70s plains).\n\nThe next concern will be next weekend. The strong EL NINO over the \nPacific is likely to continue to roar as an impressive subtropical \njet si forecast to develop and push another round of moisture towards \nthe southwest CONUS. This jet, combined with another impressive \nPacific trough should bring another round of impactful precip to the \nregion. This scenarios reflected in both the deterministic and \nstatistical guidance products (see any of the high elevation sites \non the NBM-1D viewer for next weekend). The good news is this next \nweather system should be cooler and more of the precip over our \nhigher elevations should be snow. Of course the details still need \nto be worked out, but next weekend looks like another active period \nfor the region. \\/Hodanish",
